# The Phase 3.2C and 3.2D security tests pin the exact bytes of these files, and
# those pins were recorded from a Windows checkout, where they have CRLF line
# endings. Fixing the ending here keeps every pin true on every platform (CI
# runs on Linux) without editing the packages that are pending human review.
# The committed content is unchanged; only the working-tree line ending is.
/README text eol=crlf
# Its pinned digest is the LF form, and core.autocrlf=true on a Windows
# checkout would otherwise rewrite it to CRLF and break three pin tests. That
# happened on 2026-09-20.
/README.md text eol=lf
